  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1220 AM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nThe upper ridge axis gets shifted down into Texas this weekend \ninto Monday with a weak upper wave progged to move from the \ncentral Plains into the mid- Mississippi Valley, which will likely\nkeep the surface boundary in northern Oklahoma and moderate \ntemperatures across the north on Monday. Beyond that, the \ndifferences in the patterns depicted by the medium-range models \ngive more uncertainty as we get later into the week. The \noperational GFS shows a trough moving into the Plains on Wednesday\nnight with the trough slowly moving through Thursday, while the \n12Z ECMWF still shows us underneath the eastern limb of a large \nupper ridge. Will be watching the trends over the next few days to\nsee if we will likely remain hot under the ridge or have an \nincreasing chances of storms and more seasonal temperatures mid to\nlate week.",
